PART 6: CREATING THE COMPONENTS INDEX FILE
================================================================================

WHY CREATE AN INDEX FILE?
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

An index file can simplify imports by:

• Centralizing Exports
  - Components are exported from one location

• Simplifying Import Statements
  - Consumers don't need full component file paths

• Enabling Easier Refactoring
  - Export paths can be managed centrally

• Improving Readability
  - Import statements become cleaner

• Supporting an Organized Public API
  - Clearly defines components exposed by the folder


CREATE THE INDEX FILE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

File:

src/components/index.js


CODE:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// Export Book component
export { default as Book } from './Book/Book'

// Export UserProfile component
export { default as UserProfile } from './UserProfile/UserProfile'


WHAT THIS FILE DOES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

• Exports Book

• Exports UserProfile

• Centralizes exports

• Allows App.jsx to import both components from the components directory


WITHOUT INDEX FILE:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

import Book from './components/Book/Book'
import UserProfile from './components/UserProfile/UserProfile'


WITH INDEX FILE:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

import { Book, UserProfile } from './components'


