MISTAKE 4: NOT USING PROPS
================================================================================

HARDCODED APPROACH:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// Component hardcodes book data

export default function Book() {

  const book = {
    title: 'The Great Gatsby',
    author: 'F. Scott Fitzgerald'
  }

  return (
    <h2>{book.title}</h2>
  )
}


REUSABLE APPROACH:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// Component receives data via props

export default function Book({ book }) {

  return (
    <h2>{book.title}</h2>
  )
}


WHY IT MATTERS:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

• Reusability
  - Component works with different book objects

• Flexibility
  - Component can be used in different contexts

• Testing
  - Different props can be supplied during tests

• Scalability
  - The same component can render many books


